WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:11.994
Hi! Tom has a cat, and Tom loves it. Saying the name every time is long, so English uses pronouns. Today we'll learn pronouns.

2
00:00:12.144 --> 00:00:17.682
Use I for yourself (always a capital I) and you for the person you're talking to.

3
00:00:17.832 --> 00:00:22.170
Use he for a boy or man, and she for a girl or woman.

4
00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:27.426
Use it for a thing or animal: The cat is small. It is cute.

5
00:00:27.576 --> 00:00:33.330
Use we for a group including you, and they for other people or things.

6
00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:35.898
Tom is a boy, so he.

7
00:00:36.048 --> 00:00:38.490
Mei is a girl, so she.

8
00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:40.986
Many pens, so they.

9
00:00:41.136 --> 00:00:44.658
Mum and I become we.

10
00:00:44.808 --> 00:00:48.690
Watch out! A bag is a thing, not she!

11
00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:51.378
Things and animals use it.

12
00:00:51.528 --> 00:00:55.146
So say: It is blue.

13
00:00:55.296 --> 00:01:05.250
Your turn! Sam is my friend, ___, is funny. Sam is a boy. Pause and think.

14
00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:09.978
A boy is he. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:10.128 --> 00:01:19.314
Another one! The dog is big. ___, is brown. Pause and think.

16
00:01:19.464 --> 00:01:24.042
One dog is it. Did you get it right?

17
00:01:24.192 --> 00:01:33.930
Here's another! My sister is six. ___, likes cats. Pause and think.

18
00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:38.850
A sister is she. Did you get it right?

19
00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:48.330
Try one more! Ben and Ali play. ___, are happy. Pause and think.

20
00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:53.514
Two other people: they. Did you get it right?

21
00:01:53.664 --> 00:02:02.322
Try one more! My friend and I: which pronoun? Pause and think.

22
00:02:02.472 --> 00:02:07.506
It includes me, so we. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:07.656 --> 00:02:15.522
Try one more! ___, am seven. Pause and think.

24
00:02:15.672 --> 00:02:21.882
Talking about yourself: I, with a capital. Did you get it right?

25
00:02:22.032 --> 00:02:31.458
Try one more! The books are old. ___, are on the desk. Pause and think.

26
00:02:31.608 --> 00:02:36.330
Many books: they. Did you get it right?

27
00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:45.474
Last one! Dad is tired. ___, is sleeping. Pause and think.

28
00:02:45.624 --> 00:02:50.706
Dad is a man, so he. Did you get it right?

29
00:02:50.856 --> 00:02:59.345
Remember: he for boys, she for girls, it for things and animals, we includes you, they for others, and I is always a capital.

30
00:02:59.495 --> 00:03:04.025
Use he or she to talk about your family!

